<title>CANADA: Altamira shareholder files suit to stop takeover.</title>
<headline>Altamira shareholder files suit to stop takeover.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A major shareholder of Canadian mutual fund giant Altamira Management Ltd filed suit in an Ontario court on Tuesday to stop a C$660 million takeover bid by Manufacturers Life Insurance Co Ltd.</p>
<p>AML Almiria Holdings Inc, a sister company of Almiria Capital Corp, and the founding shareholders of Altamira Management are seeking an injunction to stop Manulife which launched a C$32 per share offer on October 28.</p>
<p>Montreal-based Almiria Capital and Toronto-based Manulife each own 30.5 percent stakes in Toronto-based Altamira, Canada's 11th largest mutual fund company.</p>
</text>
